ARTWORK
The stage 1 background (assets/backgrounds/river_village.jpg), the stage 2
background (assets/backgrounds/dune_sea.jpg), the character,
pickup and effect sprites (assets/sprites/units/), the helicopter, jet, bomb,
explosion, technical and convoy sprites (assets/sprites/vehicles/), the title art, Rayan portraits, briefing dossier and travel map
(assets/ui/title_bg.jpg, rayan_portrait.png, rayan_bust.png, briefing_bg.jpg, travel_map.jpg), the weapon icons
(assets/ui/weapons/, added in 0.3.0), the first-person weapon views held in Rayan's
arms (assets/sprites/fp/, added in 0.3.1) and the app icon were
created for this project with AI image generation and then cut out and edited for
the game. They are included for use within Firebreak. The truck is still drawn in
code. All soldiers and vehicles are generic, with no flags or insignia. Weapon names
(for example "Viper 9" or "Hammer RPG") and weapon icons are original to Firebreak, carry
no maker's names, logos or markings, and are not endorsed by any manufacturer. No existing
game's characters or art are used. "Operation Wolf" is mentioned only to describe the
genre; Firebreak is not affiliated with or endorsed by its owners.

MUSIC (assets/audio/music_*.ogg, including the 0.3.1 pause-menu track music_pause.ogg
and the 0.3.6 title theme music_title_intro.ogg / music_title_intro_loop.ogg)
Music was generated with ElevenLabs Music (eleven_music_v2_5) and is used under the
ElevenLabs Music Terms (https://elevenlabs.io/music-terms). Commercial use follows
the plan in effect when the tracks were generated. On paid self-serve plans this
includes use in an Indie Game as defined in those terms (game revenue under
USD 500,000 since release, and publisher game revenue under USD 1,000,000 in the last
financial year). It does not include film, TV, radio, or Studio Game use unless the
account is on Enterprise Music. If the account is on the Free plan, credit
ElevenLabs Music (for example: "Created in collaboration with ElevenLabs"). These
tracks must not be offered as a standalone music library.

SOUND EFFECTS AND VOICE (ElevenLabs; does not include the CC0 files listed above)
Sound effects were generated with ElevenLabs Sound Effects (eleven_text_to_sound_v2),
including the 0.3.0 weapon, reload, dry-fire, cash and store sounds (prompts and credits
are listed in AUDIO_BRIEF.md).
Rayan's voice lines were generated with ElevenLabs text to speech (eleven_v4) using
the ElevenLabs Voice Library voice "Flint - Commanding Presence". All lines are
